    "diagnosis": "BIOMASS_AS_READ",
    "late_biomass_estimate_od": 0.485,
    "p_biomass_above_reading": 0.08,
    "rationale": "I diluted the retained 18 h aliquot and rescaled the readings by the dilution factor. If the reader were saturating, the rescaled values would rise above the undiluted 0.489. They didn't. The 10x dilution gave 0.0481, which scales to 0.481. The 4x dilution gave 0.1218 (two replicates, 0.1222 and 0.1214), which scales to 0.487. The single 2x reading gave 0.2613, which scales to 0.523. That is about 8% above the others and looks like a single-read outlier, since the 4x and 10x reads agree with the undiluted value. The plateau at about 0.48 from 5 h onward therefore reflects a real stationary phase, not a reader ceiling."
  },
